nts\n25. should apply block discount only to exactly 3 identical components\n26. should treat different component types (rune, moonstone) as not alike\n27. should handle two separate blocks: 3 runes and 3 moonstones -> 120 G\n28. should compute premium for newcomer's cursed sword as 165 G: (100 + 50 + 10) + 5\n2. should compute premium for long-standing customer's second contract cursed highly enchanted sword as 160 G: (100 + 50 + 30 - 20 + 10 - 15) + 5\n30. should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item in claim\n31. should compute payout for standard sword (enchantment < 8, not dragon) damage 500 G as 400 G (500 - 100)\n32. should compute payout for rune damage 200 G as 100 G (200 - 100)\n33. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum\n34. should base cap on unmodified insurance value, not on premium\n35. should not let cap increase with premium modifiers\n36. should reduce payout when claim exceeds remaining cap\n37. should exhaust cap after sufficient claims\n38. should reimburse 50% of damage for items with enchantment level >= 8\n39. should fully reimburse damage for items made of dragon material\n40. should apply enchantment 50% rule even if item is also dragon material\n41. should fully reimburse dragon-material item with enchantment < 8\n42. should reimburse 50% then deduct 100 for steel sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G -> 400 G\n43. should reimburse 400 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G: 50% of 1000 = 500, minus 100 = 400\n44. should reimburse 700 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 5 damage 800 G: full 800 minus 100 = 700\n45. should treat each damage entry as separate event with its own deductible\n46. should reject claim with more damage entries of a type than items insured\n\nTest List Phase Complete. Continuing now to the Red phase for test 1 (no stop).\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b651890ad0eb2b27","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_10-53-22_cla